A||||9||CUTTER||Any HP increase with Accell spark plug wires?||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||04-07-2000||02:15 AM||||Im putting on Accell spark plug wires on my 87 GT and woundering if they give any kind of increased Horsepower or acceleration? just put new cap and rotor on yesterday, and getting Bosche spark plugs next time its in the garage (which will be soon!!!) lol<BR>Thanks, shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||04-07-2000||02:32 AM||||Going to Accel wires and bosch plugs make the car run better and will help gas milage.<BR>In some way I'm sure this will increase horsepower but not anything really significant. You may get 1 or 2 HP out of it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||04-07-2000||07:39 AM||||I have installed Accel wires (8mm spiral core super stock) along with Bosch Platinums. Also put in Accel super coil. My theory is it don;t matter how much juice your wires and plugs carry if the coil isn't producing the big juice.  <BR>As far as performance, my calibrated Ass-O-Meter tells me that the engine revs quicker then before I did these mods. Of course, the block also had a big-ass hole in the side! Never rn the new engine with stock stuff, I just didn't want to mess with it later. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-07-2000||12:39 PM||||Ignition parts don't improve HP. They can however make the engine produce all the power it should be by providing better lightoff on the cylinder.<P>Assuming ALL stock components are good. There are a couple reasons ignition can make a motor rev higher and/or wind up quicker.<P>One is the reason above. Better lighting produces more even power from the charge.<P>another is that after market parts can be done so that they over come limitations in the OEM parts. You can add sparks like MSD boxes do. You can alter Dwell and Discharge Voltage like most coils do. Dwell is the time the coil needs to precharge to generate full voltage sparks. Faster charging coils perform better at high RPM than most OEM ones.<P>If the coil goes flat above 5000rpm then the rest of the engine does to. Doesn't matter what else the engine is capable of if the coil can't keep up.<P>In either case, you're not really getting a HP improvement. You're getting better access to the power the engine has had right allong.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-07-2000||02:20 PM||||It's kindof like how people claim they gain 5hp on the dyno with Splitfire spark plugs.  Most(if not all) of the HP is gained merely because the origional spark plugs were worn.  So if the person had just replaced the plugs with Delco, the gain would have probably been the same. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-07-2000||03:52 PM||||GTB, Exactly. I've used split fire. They didn't do anything any other brand didn't do when I put them in. They don't last any better than anything else, often not even as long. I've heard a number of complaits of broken ground legs, but mine didn't do that.<P>I stuffed some Autolite Platinum tipped in my van awhile back. Figured I'd try them once. I think I have regular Autolite in the car now. (So far as life goes Autolite has always held up best for me.)<P>Cutter,<BR>Biggest reason for buying good wires, especially on the V6, is for heat resistance. I have Borg Warner helical cores on my DIS 4. Even the 4 gets pretty hot. They've held up good. 20,000 miles on them now. You can get these lots of places. they aren't very expencive. I don't know how they would be on the V6.<P>For the V6 routing of the wires is absolutly critical. Consider Not using the OEM routing if there is another way. (Like using after market looms to hold the wires above the valve cover.)<P>Bosch says they got a design award for the +4 plugs. I can't see why. Its just a variation of "face fire" plugs that have been floating around off and on for years.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||04-07-2000||10:05 PM||||The only way those wires gave any horsepower is if the ones you replaced were toasted.<BR>I like the tri-electrode type,or surface fire spark plugs,have used them in Alfas since the early sixties.With three or more electrodes,there is always an optimum arc position available in the chamber.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||04-08-2000||03:32 PM||||I've had a set of the Borg-Warner wires on my V6 for about 1,000 miles, now.  No problems so far.  Have them routed exactly the same as oem, too.  I'll let y'all know how long they last.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||04-08-2000||08:30 PM||||So what's the take on the MSD Blaster 7.5amp Box vs MSD 6A & 6AL Multi-spark box?<P>THANKS||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||04-09-2000||10:13 AM||||I don't know what spark plugs do for hp, but always remember that yellow calipers will get you 15 hp any time! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
